 {"id": "DECIDE-1", "title": "OWNER DECISION — which navigation path to fund: give JEV the topology, or promote the controller", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 1, "depends_on": ["CTRL-WIN"], "blocks": ["NAV-MEM"], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Blocked on the owner by design; filed so the question is not lost. The evidence: the controller path reaches Route 1 in 13 cycles where JEV took ~202 episodes, but the controller costs a paid LLM call per cycle whereas JEV is the cheap tier. Option A: MEM-PROJ — wire retrieved world/* facts into state_projection.build(extra_facts=...) so the fast tier stops re-deriving topology (cheap per cycle, weeks of plumbing). Option B: promote the controller for navigation (proven, but every cycle becomes a paid call). DIST-1 is the tiebreaker if the call is close. done-when: the owner picks, and the choice is recorded as an event. falsifier: n/a — this is a decision row, not a measurement.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00"}
 {"id": "BASE-REPIN", "title": "Re-pin a fresh known-good boot state — the chained checkpoint drifted mid-run", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": ["BASE-1"], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED during T244: long_run/long_0926_0014_good.state was re-saved at 03:18 and its md5 moved from 81e4ec4e... (what BOTH baseline artifacts document) to 9b035ffc... The only surviving copy matching the documented md5 was the CTRL-WIN worktree's isolated checkpoint, rescued to data/baselines/base-1_boot.state. BASE-1 and CTRL-WIN remain reproducible from their own artifacts BECAUSE of that rescue. done-when: long runs boot from a state pinned in the repo with its md5 recorded in the baseline artifact, and a run cannot silently move it. falsifier: a future baseline cites an md5 that no longer exists on disk.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00"}
 {"id": "PERF-1", "title": "PERF: skip-on-identical-frame gate for the per-cycle screenshot save (cron_runner.py:3590) — PNG write path 5.2x cheaper, measured", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": [], "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Perf-lane measurement 2026-09-26 (measured, not a guess). Every cycle in the main run loop does Image.fromarray(screenshot).save(SCREENSHOT_DIR/f'step_{cycle+1:04d}.png') UNCONDITIONALLY at cron_runner.py:3590, even though the sibling cartographer path (cron_runner.py:3602-3651) already computes an md5 frame hash and skips re-observation on identical frames. Measured component costs on a live Emulator (data/boot.state, Oak's Lab, venv, window='null'): capture 0.251ms, PNG save 2.108ms (max 12.96ms — write stalls), RAMReader.observe() 0.058ms, emu.tick(60)=1s of game time 3.200ms. So the screenshot save is ~2.1ms of every ~5.6ms measured local cycle (~37%) — more than the emulator's frame advance and ~36x the RAM observation it exists to document. Reproduction: python3 /tmp perf scripts re-created by the perf lane (see events.jsonl PERF-1 evidence entry); component harness = boot Emulator from data/boot.state, N=50 cycles of [capture, PNG save, observe, tick(60)], report mean/median of each stage; numbers above are that output. Fix measurement (N=200 cycles, same build/state): unconditional save on a static screen 0.692ms/cycle vs md5(s.tobytes()) gate 0.080ms/cycle = 8.7x; on moving frames 0.844ms vs 0.162ms = 5.2x. Acceptance: step_*.png writes are skipped when md5(screenshot.tobytes()) equals the previous cycle's hash (or render debt/first cycle), the saved-PNG census per run stays >= the set of DISTINCT game screens (verify by re-running a boot-state cycle burst and counting files vs unique hashes), and the cartographer-side _last_frame_hash logic is reused, not duplicated — one hash per cycle, computed once. Files: cron_runner.py:3588-3590 (save), cron_runner.py:3602-3651 (existing frame-hash block). UNVERIFIED by the perf lane: interaction with BATTLE_*.png saves (line 4578) and anything downstream that assumes one PNG per cycle (e.g. make_run_video.py) — foreman must check consumers before landing.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 11:40:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/ai-plays-poke-PERF-1", "branch": "wt/PERF-1", "commit_hash": "a40b177", "worker_summary": "T249 wave: one md5 per cycle (_cycle_frame_hash) gates the step_*.png save (_save_cycle_screenshot; first cycle always saves; numbering preserved), reused by cartographer + controller cache; make_run_video gap-aware (StepFrame parsing + SRT aligned to real cycles, real ffmpeg encode on gapped frames). Census 30 cycles = 2 saves / 2 distinct hashes. BATTLE milestone untouched. Work 219d7c1, merged a40b177. Guard Tier1 PASS full.", "completed_at": "2026-09-26 13:58:00"}
