+ {"id": "TOOLS-1", "title": "S4 tool calling — the log shows >=1 model-chosen tool call with its result, and a failed call is visible to the model", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 5, "depends_on": ["MEM-POP"], "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "STAGE S4 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \"the log shows >=1 **model-chosen** tool call with its result; a failed call is visible to the model\". Measured starting point from the spec: src/core/ai_client.py does support native OpenAI function calling (tools param, tool_calls parsing, text-only-model fallback), but the controller path never uses it - it returns a JSON plan, a list of button presses - and _battle_tool_call only looks like tool use: it is a fixed translation table from JEV battle vocabulary (MOVE_n / RUN / SWITCH) to emulator transport calls, so the model is not choosing tools. Target surface (spec section 4): walk(direction, tiles), interact(target), read_dialog(), remember(key, domain, facts, applies_when), recall(key|labels|query), delegate_research(question, budget), set_goal(text, reason) / check_goal(). Rules that make the criterion checkable: the harness executes with verification, every call and its result is a decision row so the autonomy counters count tool use honestly, and a failed call surfaces its error to the model instead of silently degrading to a blind A-press. ORDERED AFTER S2 (not parallel with CTX-WIN) because two of the seven tools are remember/recall, which need the populated store and retrieval API to mean anything; S5 depends on this row because delegate_research is itself one of these model-chosen tools.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 00:45:46"}
+ {"id": "DELEG-1", "title": "S5 delegation — >=1 delegated finding written to memory and consumed in a later cycle", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 4, "depends_on": ["TOOLS-1"], "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "STAGE S5 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \">=1 delegated finding written to memory and **consumed in a later cycle**\" - and section 5 adds that acceptance requires the finding to be consumed in a LATER cycle, visible in the log, not asserted. Contract being implemented (spec section 5): delegate_research spawns a bounded subagent with max wall-clock, max tool calls and max cost; the subagent receives only the question plus declared public context and may search the web; it returns capped finding text, sources and confidence; the harness compresses the return into world/* or run/* memory and injects it into the parent's next context. Measured starting point from the spec: a grep for subagent/delegate/research across cron_runner.py and src/core/ returns nothing - there is no delegation wiring at all today. ORDERED AFTER TOOLS-1 because the only way to invoke delegation in this design is as a model-chosen tool call from the surface S4 lands, and its output must land through the memory path (S1/S2) to satisfy the 'written to memory' half of the criterion.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 00:45:46"}
+ {"id": "NAV-MEM", "title": "S6 memory-driven navigation — using world/map/* + world/path/*, cycles-to-first-map-transition drops vs the S2 baseline, and the route is cited from memory", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 4, "depends_on": ["CTX-WIN", "MEM-PROJ"], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "STAGE S6 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \"using `world/map/*` + `world/path/*`, cycles-to-first-map-transition drops vs the S2 baseline, and the route is cited from memory\". This is where the spec's headline number is spent: map_topology is 1,219 of 1,352 escalations (90%), i.e. the agent re-derives the same world fact every episode and pays a teacher call for it each time; the world/path/<from_map>-><to_map> label exists precisely to store a PROVEN traversable route plus the door tile, written when a map transition is observed, and world/map/<map_id> holds name, exits (tile + destination), landmarks and tiles visited. Both halves of the criterion are measurable: the cycle count must be compared against the baseline the S2 30-cycle run produces, and the route the agent takes must be traceable to a memory read rather than to a re-derivation. ORDERED AFTER BOTH CTX-WIN AND DELEG-1 because it consumes the window (the agent must see its own prior attempts within a run to avoid re-deriving them) and delegation (lookups about a map can arrive as a delegated finding), and it cannot be measured at all until MEM-POP has produced its baseline number; this matches the spec's chain S1 -> S2 -> {S3,S4} -> S5 -> S6. | QUORUM #1 fix 2026-09-26: dependency on DELEG-1 removed (web research is not a precondition for navigating an already-walked map) and MEM-PROJ added (memory must reach the JEV projection or this row's metric is structurally immune).", "created_at": "2026-09-26 00:45:46"}
