+ {"id": "HOLD-1", "title": "Holding a transition — the agent reaches Route 1 then walks back to Pallet Town; nothing in the plan addresses staying", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": ["CTRL-WIN"], "blocks": ["NAV-MEM"], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "CTRL-WIN measured the escape and exposed the real blocker to winning. In the isolated llm run the agent hit Route 1 at cycle 13 and was back in Pallet Town by c22, ending there (data/baselines/ctrl-win_2026-09-26.json). The S0 baseline shows the same shape: reach Route 1 at ep203, then the maps in later episodes are Pallet Town again. Escaping and STAYING are different problems, and NO stage in SPEC_agentic_memory_loop covers the second one — S6 is satisfied by a single transition. Reaching Viridian City requires crossing Route 1, which requires not regressing. Candidate causes to measure, not assert: no persistent goal state across cycles (the goal is re-sent, not tracked), no memory of 'I already came from there', and direction-locking (47% of cycles in the CTRL-WIN run) driving the agent back through the same edge. done-when: a run crosses into Route 1 and does not re-enter Pallet Town for the remainder, with the mechanism cited from the log. falsifier: the agent holds Route 1 but still cannot reach Viridian, which would move the bottleneck to the route itself.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 07:26:00"}
