+ {"id": "TOOLS-1", "title": "S4 tool calling — the log shows >=1 model-chosen tool call with its result, and a failed call is visible to the model", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 5, "depends_on": ["MEM-POP"], "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "STAGE S4 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \"the log shows >=1 **model-chosen** tool call with its result; a failed call is visible to the model\". Measured starting point from the spec: src/core/ai_client.py does support native OpenAI function calling (tools param, tool_calls parsing, text-only-model fallback), but the controller path never uses it - it returns a JSON plan, a list of button presses - and _battle_tool_call only looks like tool use: it is a fixed translation table from JEV battle vocabulary (MOVE_n / RUN / SWITCH) to emulator transport calls, so the model is not choosing tools. Target surface (spec section 4): walk(direction, tiles), interact(target), read_dialog(), remember(key, domain, facts, applies_when), recall(key|labels|query), delegate_research(question, budget), set_goal(text, reason) / check_goal(). Rules that make the criterion checkable: the harness executes with verification, every call and its result is a decision row so the autonomy counters count tool use honestly, and a failed call surfaces its error to the model instead of silently degrading to a blind A-press. ORDERED AFTER S2 (not parallel with CTX-WIN) because two of the seven tools are remember/recall, which need the populated store and retrieval API to mean anything; S5 depends on this row because delegate_research is itself one of these model-chosen tools.", "created_at": "2026-09-26 00:45:46"}
