+ {"id": "NAV-MEM", "title": "S6 memory-driven navigation — using world/map/* + world/path/*, cycles-to-first-map-transition drops vs the S2 baseline, and the route is cited from memory", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 4, "depends_on": ["CTX-WIN", "MEM-PROJ"], "blocks": [], "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "STAGE S6 of SPEC_agentic_memory_loop.md. ACCEPTANCE (verbatim from the spec): \"using `world/map/*` + `world/path/*`, cycles-to-first-map-transition drops vs the S2 baseline, and the route is cited from memory\". This is where the spec's headline number is spent: map_topology is 1,219 of 1,352 escalations (90%), i.e. the agent re-derives the same world fact every episode and pays a teacher call for it each time; the world/path/<from_map>-><to_map> label exists precisely to store a PROVEN traversable route plus the door tile, written when a map transition is observed, and world/map/<map_id> holds name, exits (tile + destination), landmarks and tiles visited. Both halves of the criterion are measurable: the cycle count must be compared against the baseline the S2 30-cycle run produces, and the route the agent takes must be traceable to a memory read rather than to a re-derivation. ORDERED AFTER BOTH CTX-WIN AND DELEG-1 because it consumes the window (the agent must see its own prior attempts within a run to avoid re-deriving them) and delegation (lookups about a map can arrive as a delegated finding), and it cannot be measured at all until MEM-POP has produced its baseline number; this matches the spec's chain S1 -> S2 -> {S3,S4} -> S5 -> S6. | QUORUM #1 fix 2026-09-26: dependency on DELEG-1 removed (web research is not a precondition for navigating an already-walked map) and MEM-PROJ added (memory must reach the JEV projection or this row's metric is structurally immune).", "created_at": "2026-09-26 00:45:46"}
